1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,590
The Financial Times used this word

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,530
in a headline about Audi.

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:05,470
Grapple.

4
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:06,590
GRAP-uhl.

5
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:08,770
Stress on the first syllable.

6
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:10,830
To grapple with something means to

7
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:13,240
struggle with a difficult problem,

8
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,610
like wrestling it.

9
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:15,550
The headline,

10
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:18,240
Audi to build a $4 billion US

11
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,170
plant as it grapples with tariffs.

12
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:23,790
Audi is wrestling with a hard problem,

13
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:24,770
tariffs.

14
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:26,830
Notice the little word after it,

15
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,290
grapple with.

16
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:28,910
At work,

17
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:29,300
try,

18
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:32,370
we're still grappling with the budget.

19
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:33,250
It's honest,

20
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,310
it says the problem is hard,

21
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:37,410
and you're working on it.

22
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:39,810
